# PROVENANCE: measured, not generated. Every response byte below was captured
# from a genuine DESFire EV3 4K over PC/SC by a PC/SC capture tool
# and is used here as an expectation for our emulator. As with the other
# hardware_physical_*.vec files, this vector is the opposite of the rest
# of the corpus: the others were recorded from the reference engine, so they
# pin what we decided; this one pins what the silicon does. A mismatch here is
# either a real divergence or a difference we can justify in writing, never a
# vector to be re-recorded from our engine.
#
# Card: UID 048222F2CF1890, hardware 51.0, software 3.0, storage 4K. Formatted
# with FormatPICC under the all-zero PICC test key, then provisioned with
# a synthetic structure whose every key is a published test key. That is what
# makes an authenticated capture safe to commit and replayable: no key material
# enters the tree, and our engine derives the same session key from the same
# pinned nonces.
#
# RndA is the fixed constant the recorder uses; RndB is the card's, recovered
# by decrypting its first authentication frame with the test key and
# pinned here with inject-random so our engine offers the same challenge.
# What this vector is for: the ISO (0x1A) handshake on a 3K3DES key, with
# its sixteen-octet challenges, measured against silicon for the first time;
# ChangeKey of the authenticated key under that session; and the refusals
# of the handshakes a 3K3DES key does not answer. GetKeyVersion after the
# change reads 55.

name: genuine EV3 4K, ISO authentication and ChangeKey on a 3K3DES key
case-id: hardware-physical-ev3-4k-3k3des-handshakes
origin: physical-card
source: captured hardware trace
requires: auth-aes
uid: 048222F2CF1890
picc-key-settings-1: 0F
picc-key-settings-2: 01
picc-auth-mode: D40
picc-key-len: 16
picc-generation: EV3
picc-storage: 4096

scan
# One application with KS2 44: four 3K3DES keys, all-zero at creation.
status   90CA000005C3C2C10F4400 => 00
#
# ISO (0x1A) on a 3K3DES key. The challenge is sixteen octets - two DES
# blocks - and the reader chains its answer from the last of them.
status   905A000003C3C2C100 => 00
inject-random 77DCA82D21FA804CF078F554EE628206
exchange native-apdu 901A0000010000 => F730C6EDEBDA7180BB61C2C2997742BC91AF
exchange native-apdu 90AF00002046FF3050A0B2218C7531511BB078AA2CEE32DAD01D716D0DEFB69EC74DC593A000 => C3CF5CF32C1D9F921C48F9274051396D9100
#
# ChangeKey on the authenticated key, to a test pattern whose three
# thirds differ. The card ends the session, so the answer has no CMAC.
exchange native-apdu 90C400002100EB9C41467B5DD76363E384AFB9E894A3D81F22CFE5B6768AC6EA0178B4CB221500 => 9100
#
# The key version a DES-family key carries in its parity bits.
exchange native-apdu 90640000010000 => 559100
#
# ISO again, under the pattern key, so the session below is genuine
# three-key 3DES and not single DES in disguise.
status   905A000003C3C2C100 => 00
inject-random FEDC6745DFC1A6F3720ED488648EABD4
exchange native-apdu 901A0000010000 => 5EAFFEDF71CD015E1B9AEEC9B1D9515691AF
exchange native-apdu 90AF00002005C021F0C1C05E34FCF057AFDFAA59F657457AB3F23CE2E7504BB80ADCBB2D4300 => C83FD62819A6747410D0FDB378A9A7CF9100
#
# The handshakes a 3K3DES key does not answer.
status   905A000003C3C2C100 => 00
exchange native-apdu 900A0000010000 => 91AE
exchange native-apdu 90AA0000010000 => 91AE
